@startuml fig11_activity_dispatch
!include theme.iuml
title Figure 11 — Activity: One Dispatch Decision

|#FAFCFB|Client|
start
:submit request\n(req_id in gRPC metadata);

|#F2F7F6|Scheduler|
:stamp arrival on the scheduler clock;
:filter nodes by admissibility\nfor this (prompt, output) bucket;
if (any admissible node?) then (no)
  :record cliff event;
  note right
    Reported separately (F-15),
    excluded from primary
    tail statistics.
  end note
  :return rejection;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:read CapabilityView **as of now - s**;
note right
  s = 0 in the default configuration;
  s > 0 is the manipulated variable of H3.
end note

:attach live queue depth and\nin-flight composition to each candidate;

switch (configured policy — one config value, F-1)
case (RoundRobin)
  :advance cursor over admissible set;
case (JSQ)
  :pick minimum queue depth;
case (StaticWeighted)
  :sample by calibrated weight,\nignoring live queue;
case (WJSQ)
  :minimise queue depth ÷ calibrated capability,\nvia CostModel.expected_service_time();
case (Threshold T)
  :round-robin over nodes\nwith capability > T;
endswitch

:write DecisionRecord —\nqueue depths, capability estimates,\nestimate ages, candidate scores (F-3);
:dispatch to chosen node;

|#FAFCFB|Worker|
:enqueue;
:hand to engine's running batch;
:generate full response;
:emit worker record;

|#FAFCFB|Client|
:receive response directly from worker (F-11);
:emit client record;
stop

legend bottom
  Every branch above shares one interface and one admissible set,
  so **policy is the only factor that varies** across a comparison (F-2, F-14).
endlegend
@enduml
